    "destination": "/privacy",
    "categories": [],
    "tags": [],
    "excerpt": "IBAA.org is committed to protecting your privacy and developing technology that gives you the most powerful and safe online experience. This Statement of Privacy applies to the IBAA.org site and governs data collection and usage. By using the IBAA.org site, you consent to the data practices described in this statement. Collection of your Personal Information […]",
    "body": [
      "IBAA.org is committed to protecting your privacy and developing technology that gives you the most powerful and safe online experience. This Statement of Privacy applies to the IBAA.org site and governs data collection and usage. By using the IBAA.org site, you consent to the data practices described in this statement.",
      "Collection of your Personal Information",
      "IBAA.org collects personally identifiable information, such as your email address, name, home or work address or telephone number. IBAA.org also collects anonymous demographic information, which is not unique to you, such as your ZIP code, age, gender, preferences, interests and favorites. There is also information about your computer hardware and software that is automatically collected by IBAA.org. This information can include: your IP address, browser type, domain names, access times and referring website addresses. This information is used by IBAA.org for the operation of the service, to maintain quality of the service, and to provide general statistics regarding use of the IBAA.org site. Please keep in mind that if you directly disclose personally identifiable information or personally sensitive data through IBAA.org public message boards, this information may be collected and used by others. Note: IBAA.org does not read any of your private online communications.",
      "Use of your Personal Information",
      "IBAA.org encourages you to review the privacy statements of Web sites you choose to link to from IBAA.org so that you can understand how those Web sites collect, use and share your information. IBAA.org is not responsible for the privacy statements or other content on Web sites outside of the IBAA.org and IBAA.org family of Web sites. IBAA.org collects and uses your personal information to operate the IBAA.org Web site and deliver the services you have requested. IBAA.org also uses your personally identifiable information to inform you of other products or services available from IBAA.org and its affiliates. IBAA.org may also contact you via surveys to conduct research about your opinion of current services or of potential new services that may be offered.",
      "IBAA.org does not sell, rent or lease its customer lists to third parties. IBAA.org may, from time to time, contact you on behalf of external business partners about a particular offering that may be of interest to you. In those cases, your unique personally identifiable information (e-mail, name, address, telephone number) is not transferred to the third party. In addition, IBAA.org may share data with trusted partners to help us perform statistical analysis, send you email or postal mail, provide customer support, or arrange for deliveries. All such third parties are prohibited from using your personal information except to provide these services to IBAA.org, and they are required to maintain the confidentiality of your information.",
      "IBAA.org does not use or disclose sensitive personal information, such as race, religion, or political affiliations, without your explicit consent. IBAA.org keeps track of the Web sites and pages our customers visit within IBAA.org, in order to determine what IBAA.org services are the most popular. This data is used to deliver customized content and advertising within IBAA.org to customers whose behavior indicates that they are interested in a particular subject area. IBAA.org Web sites will disclose your personal information, without notice, only if required to do so by law or in the good faith belief that such action is necessary to: (a) conform to the edicts of the law or comply with legal process served on IBAA.org or the site; (b) protect and defend the rights or property of IBAA.org; and, (c) act under exigent circumstances to protect the personal safety of users of IBAA.org, or the public.",
      "Security of your Personal Information",
      "IBAA.org secures your personal information from unauthorized access, use or disclosure. IBAA.org secures the personally identifiable information you provide on computer servers in a controlled, secure environment, protected from unauthorized access, use or disclosure. When personal information (such as a credit card number) is transmitted to other Web sites, it is protected through the use of encryption, such as the Secure Socket Layer (SSL) protocol.",
      "Changes to this Statement",
      "IBAA.org will occasionally update this Statement of Privacy to reflect company and customer feedback. IBAA.org encourages you to periodically review this Statement to be informed of how IBAA.org is protecting your information. IBAA.org welcomes your comments regarding this Statement of Privacy. If you believe that IBAA.org has not adhered to this Statement, please use the contact form on this website and we will use commercially reasonable efforts to promptly determine and remedy the problem."
    ],
